ike how the workerref is kept right now.\n2. Closing mInput also on the window teardown, to prevent memory leak as Fetch does not close the stream automatically.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195132\n\nDepends on D195131", "files": ["dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.cpp", "dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/FileAPI/blob/Blob-stream.any.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4f68f28638b4600ee59d2f4bdb58306f5e19abe6", "parents": ["d58a03e236faae658fd5ef016b89b43509e9c04e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1701374901, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "179": {"changesets": [{"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1837268, update inline spellchecker when text data is modified,  a=RyanVM\n\nUsing the test for bug 1602526 as the basis for the new test but tweaking it by\nadding the event listener used in the first testcase of the bug.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184987\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195233", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.h", "editor/spellchecker/tests/mochitest.ini", "editor/spellchecker/tests/test_bug1837268.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "552e49e9a6a5f26452ef2ed92b3bf2fbe8d8271d", "parents": ["4f68f28638b4600ee59d2f4bdb58306f5e19abe6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1701448901, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "180": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840144 - clean up some TLS socket creation error handling  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D193722\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195287", "files": ["dom/indexedDB/ActorsParent.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/NSSSock