p has run. r=calixte, a=RyanVM\n\nBackport of upstream PR:\nhttps://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js/pull/17106\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195741", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4f1beaeafa0822cfbee57cef79a6bc2fc0473c73", "parents": ["ca7e608913e933cd45c85a3767acc08e889619f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1861349 - Allow resizing certManager columns. r=settings-reviewers,Gijs a=RyanVM\n\nSee also bug 1821404.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192058", "files": ["security/manager/pki/resources/content/certManager.css", "security/manager/pki/resources/content/certManager.xhtml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fce67958ff6ed8a4deb12916dc5beba591cca0e2", "parents": ["4f1beaeafa0822cfbee57cef79a6bc2fc0473c73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1862599 - Don't let certmanager treecol intrinsic sizes affect its minimum size. r=Gijs, a=RyanVM\n\nOtherwise the minimum size grows once you shrink a column under the\ntreecol label size.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192555", "files": ["security/manager/pki/resources/content/certManager.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f8d65aab1b47b2e4bf14f42c39737ba49365613c", "parents": ["fce67958ff6ed8a4deb12916dc5beba591cca0e2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1701959557, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "192": {"changesets": [{"author": "Issam Mani \u003cimani@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1864379 - P1. Don't dispatch LoginManager DOM events for disconnected input elements.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D194768\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195780", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLFormElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLFormElement.h", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.h", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.h", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginManagerChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8c2fb224d0e4f45029ce6935d003bfabd37e9bd3", "parents": ["f8d65aab1b47b2e4bf14f42c39737ba49365613c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Issam Mani \u003cimani@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1864379 - P2. Fix failing tests.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D194769\n\nDepends on D195780\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195781", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/browser/browser_DOMFormHasPassword.js", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/browser/browser_DOMFormHasPossibleUsername.js", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/browser/browser_DOMInputPasswordAdded.js", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/mochitest/test_formless_autofill.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8f268907679ae83c22737319b7ae6064dddbd9a4", "parents": ["8c2fb224d0e4f45029ce6935d003bfabd37e9bd3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Issam Mani \u003cimani@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1864379 - P3. Remove obsolete PWMGR_PASSWORD_INPUT_IN_FORM telemetry probe.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D194770\n\nDepends on D195781\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195782", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json", "toolkit/components/telemetry/histogram-allowlists.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e32000c11dcafbf73a96f714eb8c39fff30d4fe6", "parents": ["8f268907679ae83c22737319b7ae6064dddbd9a4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1701959995, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "193": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1864123 - Optimize flushing to base stream; r=dom-storage,asuth a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D193286\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195046", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptingOutputStream.h", "dom/quota/EncryptingOutputStream_impl.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b66eb4c63b104d4784c04a3a76cfcb5df6bbdd08", "parents": ["e32000c11dcafbf73a96f714eb8c39fff30d4fe6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1442018 - Avoid crashing in BCPaintBorderIterator if mCellMap was not found. r=layout-reviewers,emilio a=RyanVM\n\nThis does not fix the underlying issue, which is that when the table\ngot fragmented, we failed to maintain the cellmap (attached to the\nfirst-in-flow) to keep track of the additional rowgroup frame created\nto go in the overflowing part of the table.\n\nSo this is a wallpaper patch just to prevent the crash here (confirmed\nwith testcase 5); it'll still throw NS_ASSERTIONs in a debug build,\nand in the \"bad\" case (which depends on details of scaling) some of\nthe borders will be missing from the print preview/output, but that\nseems preferable to crashing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D193660", "files": ["layout/tables/nsTableFrame.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "00c37855c811903634e1d84fa2a6d85b3eea5a7d", "parents": ["b66eb4c63b104d4784c04a3a76cfcb5df6bbdd08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1442018 - nsCellMap needs to try harder to find the appropriate cellmap for a table header/footer that may be a repeat. r=layout-reviewers,emilio a=RyanVM\n\nIf a repeated header/footer row group gets fragmented, so that it has a\nnext-in-flow, its REPEATABLE flag will be cleared. But in such a case,\nnsCellMap still needs to find the \"original\" in order to get the map\nfor the repeated frame.\n\nDepends on D193660\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D193661", "files": ["layout/tables/nsCellMap.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dc171969cb1698e54f159ddc6e24ce781ca03a29", "parents": ["00c37855c811903634e1d84fa2a6d85b3eea5a7d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1442018 - Add testcase-5 as a crashtest. r=layout-reviewers,emilio a=RyanVM\n\nDepends on D193661\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D193662", "files": ["layout/base/crashtests/1442018-1.html", "layout/base/crashtests/crashtests.list"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "649711a0d9db14ac59e7e73059a3c9ff11cbc12f", "parents": ["dc171969cb1698e54f159ddc6e24ce781ca03a29"], "tags": []}], "date": 1701964797, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "194": {"changesets": [{"author": "Karl Tomlinson \u003ckarlt+@karlt.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1858509 add thread-safety annotations around MediaSourceDemuxer::mMonitor  a=RyanVM\n\nmDemuxers array elements are also removed when no longer required.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D193616\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195746", "files": ["dom/media/mediasource/MediaSourceDemuxer.cpp", "dom/media/mediasource/MediaSourceDemuxer.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fbd8ce659fc671fc9039ac45bdaf3f867b92a719", "parents": ["649711a0d9db14ac59e7e73059a3c9ff11cbc12f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1701976525, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "195": {"changesets": [{"author": "Barret Rennie \u003cbarret@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1796023 - Compare return value of readlink in nsLocalFileUnix::GetNativeTarget r=xpcom-reviewers,nika a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D190987", "files": ["xpcom/io/nsLocalFileUnix.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fc9295544e5fa95196bb9732a733c09b92d33f59", "parents": ["fbd8ce659fc671fc9039ac45bdaf3f867b92a719"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morgan Rae Reschenberg \u003cmreschenberg@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1851441: Speculative fix for image map/html area element crash r=Jamie, a=RyanVM\n\nI think this crash may occur when the image map is being removed or when the area element is being moved.\nIn any case, I'm reasonably confident that the reason for this crash was a null boundingFrame passed to TransformRect, which should only happen when the image map doesn't exist / has no frame.\n\nAlso, we really shouldn't be transforming anyway, so I\u2019ve removed the transform call.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D193460", "files": ["accessible/html/HTMLImageMapAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e3a36f826d1b52f6057808fe887e11d769aee801", "parents": ["fc9295544e5fa95196bb9732a733c09b92d33f59"], "tags": []}], "date": 1701999905, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "196": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1858033 - Refactor Proxy::mXMLHttpRequestPrivate to become a WeakPtr and simplify Teardown/Unpin.  a=RyanVM\n\nThis patch also clarifies that mXMLHttpRequestPrivate is only ever dereferenced on the worker thread\nand avoids to copy its raw pointer on the main thread by relying always on Proxy to access it.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D194077\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195826", "files": ["dom/xhr/XMLHttpRequestWorker.cpp", "dom/xhr/XMLHttpRequestWorker.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a7b220657c36dc99f6118d9e51a542d8cc45663d", "parents": ["e3a36f826d1b52f6057808fe887e11d769aee801"], "tags": []}], "date": 1702004160, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "197": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1857742 - patch 1 - Vendor the oxilangtag crate into third_party/rust. r=supply-chain-reviewers,dholbert a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195822", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "third_party/rust/oxilangtag/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/oxilangtag/CHANGELOG.md", "third_party/rust/oxilangtag/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/oxilangtag/LICENSE", "third_party/rust/oxilangtag/README.md", "third_party/rust/oxilangtag/benches/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/oxilangtag/deny.toml", "third_party/rust/oxilangtag/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/oxilangtag/tests/lib.rs", "toolkit/library/rust/shared/Cargo.toml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "38048644c5b70354ca764fcb23d3b9a547af168f", "parents": ["a7b220657c36dc99f6118d9e51a542d8cc45663d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1857742 - patch 2 - Use oxilangtag rather than unic_langid to parse lang tags for nsStyleUtil::LangTagCompare. r=layout-reviewers,dholbert,TYLin a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195823\n\nDepends on D195822", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "intl/locale/moz.build", "intl/locale/rust/oxilangtag-ffi/Cargo.toml", "intl/locale/rust/oxilangtag-ffi/cbindgen.toml", "intl/locale/rust/oxilangtag-ffi/src/lib.rs", "layout/style/nsStyleUtil.cpp", "toolkit/library/rust/shared/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/library/rust/shared/lib.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e403ece4ee4ff8bd57a897d95e08f7554014edc3", "parents": ["38048644c5b70354ca764fcb23d3b9a547af168f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1857742 - patch 3 - Add some more :lang()-matching reftests. r=layout-reviewers,dholbert a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195824\n\nDepends on D195823", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/selectors-4/lang-020.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/selectors-4/lang-021.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/selectors-4/lang-022.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/selectors-4/lang-023.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/selectors-4/lang-024.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/selectors-4/lang-025.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7f7abd40390b60e289472c60c89a741b92f28c4a", "parents": ["e403ece4ee4ff8bd57a897d95e08f7554014edc3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865482 - Make CSS :lang() matching more correctly follow the BCP4647 Extended Filtering algorithm. r=layout-reviewers,emilio a=RyanVM\n\nThe matching behavior implemented in bug 1857742 did not quite follow the spec,\nparticularly with regard to language *ranges* (as used in the :lang() pseudo)\nthat are not themselves valid language *tags*.\n\nThis updates the LangTagCompare function to more correctly follow the BCP4647\n\"Extended Filtering\" algorithm, and adjusts the relevant WPT tests (originally\nfrom bug 1857742) to reflect the corrected behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D194054", "files": ["intl/locale/rust/oxilangtag-ffi/src/lib.rs", "layout/style/nsStyleUtil.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/selectors-4/lang-021.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/selectors-4/lang-023.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/selectors-4/lang-024.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b7218284895a39661a84a42f527df314e9e6335f", "parents": ["7f7abd40390b60e289472c60c89a741b92f28c4a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1702049653, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "198": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1863039: Fail gracefully in nsAccUtils::GetScreenCoordsForWindow if OuterDocOfRemoteBrowser returns null.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192812\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195993", "files": ["accessible/base/nsAccUtils.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "13263e1bb0dab92aa4b37fc049dbb40dfbacf182", "parents": ["b7218284895a39661a84a42f527df314e9e6335f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1702251844, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "199": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1863466: Support details and error message relations for RemoteAccessible.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192916\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195992", "files": ["accessible/base/CacheConstants.h", "accessible/generic/LocalAccessible.cpp", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_caching_relations.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "08db0914a0737c2166ee1f91b63b44e8d4cab8dc", "parents": ["13263e1bb0dab92aa4b37fc049dbb40dfbacf182"], "tags": []}], "date": 1702251887, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "200": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1861902: Enforce some table restrictions to avoid crashes and improve consistency.  a=RyanVM\n\n1. Never treat a cell in a nested CachedTableAccessible as a cell in the outer table. This could previously result in trying to use cache data from one CachedTableAccessible when querying another, which could cause crashes.\n2. Don't create an HTMLTableRowAccessible when the \u003ctr\u003e has a valid ARIA role other than \"row\". This could previously result in a situation where \u003ctr role=\"grid\"\u003e was treated as a row by its parent table, but the \u003ctr\u003e was also treated as a separate table.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192175\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D196001", "files": ["accessible/base/CachedTableAccessible.cpp", "accessible/base/HTMLMarkupMap.h", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_caching_table.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "eac39ae2de2c44dff3ed6caab46e1c201a05f93d", "parents": ["08db0914a0737c2166ee1f91b63b44e8d4cab8dc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1702301767, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "201": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D196028", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/onecrl.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "584ca177d864aeda439e886b7b30a6c21dcdcc97", "parents": ["eac39ae2de2c44dff3ed6caab46e1c201a05f93d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1709082 - Block legacy DLL for digital signatures with ID card from Spain. r=win-reviewers,keeler,gstoll a=RyanVM\n\nThis patch blocks UsrDNIeCertStore.dll which was formerly used for\ndigital signatures in the software packages for spanish ID cards (DNIe).\nThis DLL is old and produces recurrent crashes for users who have it\ninstalled. The new software packages distribute and use DNIe_P11_x64.dll\ninstead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195533", "files": ["toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/WindowsDllBlocklistDefs.in"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "079f307073da35977aeb555a927556db958925d8", "parents": ["584ca177d864aeda439e886b7b30a6c21dcdcc97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1868901. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D195888", "files": ["widget/GfxDriverInfo.cpp", "widget/GfxDriverInfo.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3c6e8e9d0084eee6528d0c3f934ac13d42518680", "parents": ["079f307073da35977aeb555a927556db958925d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1838286 - Fix a race condition with in-process DLL interception. r=win-reviewers,gstoll, a=RyanVM\n\nIf a thread starts running a detoured function right after we\nsuccessfully committed our 13-bytes patch, there is a short delay where\nit can reach the patched_XXX function and try to call stub_XXX while\nstub_XXX.mOrigFunc is still a null pointer.\n\nWe fix this specific race condition, which, in the current code base,\nmaterializes mostly as crashes in patched_BaseThreadInitThunk when\ntrying to call stub_BaseThreadInitThunk.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192668", "files": ["toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/interceptor/PatcherDetour.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5722386fbf57d951d16013df566d8aa58211abed", "parents": ["3c6e8e9d0084eee6528d0c3f934ac13d42518680"], "tags": []}], "date": 1702305879, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "202": {"changesets": [{"author": "Brad Werth \u003cbwerth@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1854820: Make the transition to window normal state work the same on extension windows as it does elsewhere. r=extension-reviewers,robwu a=RyanVM\n\nCalling window.restore will return the window to its previous\ndimensions. Prior to this patch, extension windows transitioning to\nnormal state would add a second step where they would forcibly resize\nthe window to content. The motivating reason for this additional step is\nsome kind of difficulty with macOS windows restoring from other states.\nThose issues were handled comprehensively in Bug 1631735, and now the\nextra step is unnecessary and surprising to users. Since the call was\nbeing made potentially during a deminimization native transition, the\nwindow is at a very small size and expanding it to fit the content is\nresizing it to a strange small size. Window.restore will do the right\nthing, so this patch stops calling sizeToContent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D189972", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-browser.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6327ae0fdd2168756f77745807669b27382e5a82", "parents": ["5722386fbf57d951d16013df566d8aa58211abed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brad Werth \u003cbwerth@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1854820 Part 2: Update an extension window test to check window sizes. r=extension-reviewers,robwu a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192980", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_windows_update.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "aa9f02961b2bbb92e17fea5d6b8fd14c097baf72", "parents": ["6327ae0fdd2168756f77745807669b27382e5a82"], "tags": ["FIREFOX_115_6_0esr_BUILD1", "FIREFOX_115_6_0esr_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1702313184, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}}
}";